    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: GOLD membership tier for 3+ member households\n\nThe `membershipTier` was derived purely in `OwnerMapper` and only ever produced `SILVER`/`BRONZE`, with no notion of household size. Following the existing pattern for derived-at-creation fields (like `namesakeCount`), I added a persisted household-size snapshot computed during the create pipeline and taught the mapper to emit `GOLD`.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdSize.java`** (new) \u2014 a pipeline step that counts existing owners sharing this owner's `householdId` and adds 1 for the owner being created (a solo/no-householdId owner is a household of 1). It runs after `AssignHouseholdId` sets the id and before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner is counted exactly once.\n\n3. **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignHouseholdSize` step (under `transaction` governance) between `assignNamesake` and `assignBulkWarning`.\n\n4. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier` now yields `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE rule.\n\n5. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `household_size INTEGER` column; updated `hsqldb/data.sql`'s positional seed inserts with the extra `NULL`.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` description to document the GOLD rule.\n\nThe spec semantics \u2014 \"3+ members **after this create**\" \u2014 are captured as a snapshot taken at creation time (consistent with how `namesakeCount` works). The acceptance test `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` (build a 3-member shared household, assert the third member is GOLD) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
